    # High-duration dependency envelope, not a fabricated fixed-date calendar.
    timeline=''.join(f'<div class="schedule-row"><span>{esc(p["phase"])}</span><div class="schedule-track"><div class="schedule-bar" style="margin-left:{pro_timing[p["id"]]["start_high"]/pro_weeks[1]*100:.2f}%;width:{(pro_timing[p["id"]]["finish_high"]-pro_timing[p["id"]]["start_high"])/pro_weeks[1]*100:.2f}%"></div></div><small>week {pro_timing[p["id"]]["start_high"]+1:.0f}–{math.ceil(pro_timing[p["id"]]["finish_high"]):.0f}</small></div>' for p in phases)
    context_links=' · '.join(f'<a href="{esc(r["url"])}">{esc(r["trade"])}</a>' for r in cfg['rate_context'])
    document=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Construction materials, labor & time · Portal Earthship</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/site.css?v=construction-2"></head><body><main><nav><a href="../index.html">← Design overview</a><a href="us-purchasing-and-costs.csv">Materials CSV</a><a href="labor-and-schedule.csv">Labor / schedule CSV</a><a href="cost-breakdown.md">Full document</a></nav><header><p class="eyebrow">HOUSE CONSTRUCTION · {rates['date']}</p><h1>Materials, labor & build time.</h1><p class="lede">Land and off-grid power already acquired. Focus on building the house.</p></header><div class="metrics"><article><span>House materials</span><strong>{money(mat[0])}–{money(mat[1])}</strong></article><article><span>Hired trade labor</span><strong>{money(paid[0])}–{money(paid[1])}</strong></article><article><span>Machinery / forms / pump / lift</span><strong>{money(equip[0])}–{money(equip[1])}</strong></article><article><span>Hired-crew construction time</span><strong>{pro_weeks[0]}–{pro_weeks[1]} weeks</strong></article></div><p class="notice">{esc(scope)} Estimates, not invoices or contractor bids. Freight, tax, fees and cash contingency remain separate. Optional patio excluded.</p><section><h2>Different ways to staff the build</h2>{option_table}<p>Totals include the same house materials and construction equipment. The GC option alone adds a separate coordination fee. Owner-assisted labor savings require {span(*owner_hours)} hours of owner work, at 40 combined team hours/week; elapsed time changes accordingly. Owner project-management time is additional.</p><p>Reference direct house construction: <b>{money(direct[0])}–{money(direct[1])}</b> before separately listed freight, tax, fees and reserves.</p><p><a href="labor-options.csv">Download scenario comparison</a> · <a href="overall-budget.csv">Direct construction summary CSV</a></p></section><section id="labor"><h2>Trade labor and effort</h2><p>{esc(rate_context)}</p><p>{context_links}</p>{phase_table}<p><b>{span(*hours)} total person-hours</b>. A 4-person crew working 40 hours each supplies 160 person-hours; labor cost is person-hours × per-worker billable rate. Crew size affects duration, not a second cost multiplier.</p></section><section id="schedule"><h2>Rough build sequence</h2><p>{esc(estimate['schedule_basis'])}</p><p class="small">Bars show the longer-duration hired-crew dependency scenario. They include phase waits but not the final 4-week coordination buffer. Week labels are rounded planning windows, not promised start dates.</p><div class="schedule-chart">{timeline}</div><p><a href="labor-and-schedule.csv">Download hours, crews, dependencies and timing</a></p><details><summary>Detailed labor / schedule assumptions</summary><ul>{''.join('<li>'+esc(x)+'</li>' for x in assumptions)}</ul></details></section><section><h2>Equipment kept separate from labor</h2>{eq_table}</section><section><h2>House material purchase breakdown</h2><p>US dressed stock sizes and units throughout. Advertised supplier benchmarks and authored allowances remain labeled. Net quantities, waste and purchase rounding are in the CSV. These are not yet local purchase quotes or a cut list.</p>{material_table}</section><section><h2>Separate from the construction headline</h2>{extra_table}<p>Septic, well/water supply and long off-house service trenches are unpriced here. They are not assumed acquired merely because land and power are acquired. A functioning water/wastewater arrangement remains necessary for occupancy.</p><p><a href="separate-budget-items.csv">Separate-items CSV</a> · <a href="optional-materials.csv">Optional patio material CSV</a></p><h3>Exclusions / open scope</h3><ul>{''.join('<li>'+esc(x)+'</li>' for x in excluded)}</ul></section><footer>Draft A · All amounts USD · Supplier price check {rates['date']} · <a href="cost-breakdown.md">Full report with purchasing qualifications and evidence</a></footer></main></body></html>'''
    (root/'materials/costs.html').write_text(document,encoding='utf-8')
    print(json.dumps({k:estimate[k] for k in ['material_low_usd','material_high_usd','labor_low_usd','labor_high_usd','labor_person_hours_low','labor_person_hours_high','overall_low_usd','overall_high_usd','calendar_weeks_low','calendar_weeks_high']},indent=2))
